#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.is_alive:4
#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:35
#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.wait_for:6 of
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.is_alive:5 of
msgid "bool or None"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.is_alive:6 of
msgid ""
"``True``/``False``, or ``None`` when liveness cannot be determined (no "
"PID was reported, or the query itself failed). ``None`` must never be "
"read as \"dead\" — an unanswerable question is not a negative answer, and"
" killing a healthy multi-hour job over a transient query failure would be"
" far worse than waiting."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:1 of
msgid "Block until *handle* finishes, dies, or *timeout_s* elapses."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:3 of
msgid ""
"Two independent signals are consulted, because neither alone is "
"sufficient:"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:6 of
msgid ""
"**The rc sentinel** is authoritative for *completion* — the launcher "
"writes it only after the solver has exited — but it says nothing when the"
" process is killed before reaching that line (a reboot, an OOM kill, "
"someone else's ``taskkill``).  On its own it would leave the poll loop "
"waiting out the entire timeout for a job that died minutes in, which is "
"precisely the wrong trade for jobs measured in hours."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:13 of
msgid ""
"**Process liveness** covers that gap, and deliberately does *not* impose "
"a deadline: a job that is still running is still running, no matter how "
"long it has taken.  A single direct-solver factorization can occupy an "
"hour writing nothing at all, so elapsed time and file growth are both "
"useless as health signals here — only the process itself is trustworthy."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:20 of
msgid ""
"The two race: the solver can exit between the rc read and the liveness "
"check, so an apparent death is confirmed by re-reading the sentinel after"
" *settle_s* rather than reported immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:26 of
msgid "timeout_s"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:-1 of
msgid "float or None"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:27 of
msgid ""
"Wall-clock cap.  ``None`` means none — with liveness detection in place "
"that is a reasonable default for long solves, since a dead job is caught "
"within one poll interval regardless."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:30 of
msgid "settle_s"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:-1 of
msgid "float"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:31 of
msgid ""
"Grace given to a just-finished launcher to flush its sentinel before "
"\"the process is gone\" is treated as a death."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:36
#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.wait_for:7 of
msgid "tuple[str, int | None, float]"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.base.ExecutionBackend.wait:37 of
msgid ""
"``(verdict, returncode, elapsed)`` with *verdict* one of ``'finished'`` /"
" ``'died'`` / ``'timeout'``."
msgstr ""

