msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend:6 of
msgid ""
"When given, contexts are remapped to ``<work_root>/<job_name>`` instead "
"of running in place.  Used by tests to exercise the staging path without "
"a network; ``None`` (the default) leaves every context untouched, which "
"is what production uses."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.map_context:1 of
msgid "Apply this host's overrides; otherwise hand *ctx* straight back."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.map_context:3 of
msgid ""
"A plain ``LocalBackend()`` returns the identical object, so a host-less "
"batch is byte-for-byte the behaviour it always had.  A local "
":class:`~ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec` may still override "
"``cpus_per_job``, which is what lets a mixed pool give this machine a "
"different job width from the remote ones."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.probe_cores:1 of
msgid ""
"Physical cores on this machine — the same measurement a host-less batch "
"has always used, so both paths report the same number."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.submit_detached:1 of
msgid "Launch with process-group isolation and keep the live handle."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.submit_detached:3 of
msgid ""
"Locally there is no reason to detach-and-poll: holding the real "
":class:`~subprocess.Popen` gives the terminate ladder a precise process "
"group to reach ``standard.exe`` through, which is strictly better than a "
"PID scraped out of WMI.  The rc sentinel is still written so both "
"backends expose the same completion signal."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.is_alive:1 of
msgid "Whether the launched process is still running."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.is_alive:3 of
msgid ""
"Answered from the live :class:`~subprocess.Popen` when this backend "
"started it.  Without one — a resumed session, say — liveness is genuinely"
" unknown, and ``None`` says so rather than guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.wait:1 of
msgid "Block on the real process handle rather than polling a file."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.LocalBackend.wait:3 of
msgid ""
"Locally we own a live :class:`~subprocess.Popen`, so waiting on it "
"returns the instant the solver exits.  Falling back to the base class's "
"poll loop would add up to *max_interval* seconds of latency per job for "
"no benefit."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.resolve_local_exe:1 of
msgid "Absolute path for *exe* on this machine, honouring ``PATHEXT``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.resolve_local_exe:3 of
msgid ""
"``subprocess`` launches through ``CreateProcess``, which searches "
"``PATH`` but **not** ``PATHEXT`` — it only ever appends ``.exe``.  So a "
"bare ``'abaqus'`` fails with ``FileNotFoundError: [WinError 2]`` even on "
"a machine where ``abaqus.bat`` is properly on ``PATH`` and "
":func:`shutil.which` finds it.  The error names no file, which makes it "
"needlessly hard to place."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.resolve_local_exe:10 of
msgid ""
"Resolving up front removes the trap.  Anything that already looks like a "
"path is returned untouched, and an unresolvable name is returned as-is so"
" the caller can report it verbatim."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.wait_for:1 of
msgid "Poll *handle* until it finishes or *timeout_s* elapses."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.wait_for:3 of
msgid "Shared by both backends so the completion semantics cannot drift."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.local.wait_for:8 of
msgid ""
"``(verdict, returncode, elapsed)`` where *verdict* is ``'finished'`` or "
"``'timeout'``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.backends.rst:24
msgid "ABQflow.core.backends.recording module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording:1 of
msgid "RecordingBackend — dry-run the remote path with no network and no mocks."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording:3 of
msgid ""
"Extends the ``record_only`` idea that :class:`AbaqusRunner` already "
"ships: commands are recorded instead of executed, and the poll sequence "
"can be scripted, so the whole remote pipeline — staging, launcher "
"generation, poll loop, fetch, diagnose — is exercisable in a unit test."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording:8 of
msgid ""
"Shipped in the package rather than kept in the test tree, because a "
"remote dry-run is useful to users for the same reason ``record_only`` is."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:1 of
msgid "Record every command and file operation; execute nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:6 of
msgid ""
"When set, contexts are remapped under it, so path mapping is exercised "
"exactly as a remote backend would."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:8 of
msgid "poll_sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:-1 of
msgid "list[int | None] or None"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:9 of
msgid ""
"Return codes handed out by successive :meth:`poll` calls, e.g. ``[None, "
"None, 0]`` for \"running, running, finished\".  Exhausting the list "
"yields the last value forever.  ``None`` (the default) means every poll "
"reports success immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:13 of
msgid "name"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend:14 of
msgid "Identifier reported as the backend name."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend.run:1 of
msgid "Record *cmd* and answer with a well-formed hook payload."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend.run:3 of
msgid ""
"Emitting the sentinel block rather than empty output is what lets this "
"backend drive :meth:`AbaqusRunner.run_hook` end to end — argument "
"mapping, interpreter selection, sidecar fetch ordering — without a "
"network.  Set ``hook_results`` to script the values it returns."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend.is_alive:1 of
msgid "Hand out the next scripted liveness answer; the last one persists."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.recording.RecordingBackend.commands:1 of
msgid "Recorded command lines, optionally filtered by *stage*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/ABQflow.core.backends.rst:31
msgid "ABQflow.core.backends.ssh module"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh:1 of
msgid "SshBackend — run Abaqus on another Windows machine over SSH + SFTP."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh:3 of
msgid ""
"``paramiko`` is imported lazily, inside :meth:`SshBackend.connect`, so a "
"local-only installation never needs it and ``import ABQflow`` keeps "
"working without it.  Install with ``pip install 'ABQflow[remote]'``."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh:8 of
msgid "Threading"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh:9 of
msgid ""
"One backend instance belongs to one job and therefore to one worker "
"thread. paramiko's ``Transport`` tolerates concurrent channel opens, but "
"a single ``SFTPClient`` does **not**, so nothing here is shared between "
"threads. Remote jobs are I/O-bound on this side — upload, launch, sleep, "
"stat, download — which is why the remote path uses threads rather than "
"processes (and incidentally sidesteps the fact that an ``SSHClient`` "
"cannot be pickled into a ``ProcessPoolExecutor``)."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:1 of
msgid ""
"Execute on a remote Windows machine described by a "
":class:`~ABQflow.core.hosts.HostSpec`."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:5 of
msgid "host"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:-1 of
msgid "HostSpec"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:6 of
msgid "Target machine.  Must have ``hostname`` and ``work_root`` set."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:7 of
msgid "logger"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:-1 of
msgid "logging.Logger or None"
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend:8 of
msgid "Optional logger for connection events."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.connect:1 of
msgid "Open the SSH connection, importing paramiko on first use."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.reconnect:1 of
msgid "Re-establish a dropped connection."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.reconnect:3 of
msgid ""
"Always safe: every completion signal lives in a file on the remote disk, "
"so a poll loop resumes with nothing lost."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.map_context:1 of
msgid "Rewrite *ctx* to the remote job directory and this host's Abaqus."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.map_context:3 of
msgid ""
"One :func:`dataclasses.replace` handles both the path problem and the "
"\"Abaqus lives elsewhere on that machine\" problem, because every derived"
" path on :class:`~ABQflow.core.context.JobContext` is a property computed"
" from ``output_dir``.  The command builders therefore need no changes and"
" ``JobContext`` stays frozen and local-first."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.probe_cores:1 of
msgid "Physical cores on the remote machine, measured over SSH."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.probe_cores:3 of
msgid ""
"``Win32_Processor.NumberOfCores`` summed over sockets is the physical "
"count, matching what ``psutil.cpu_count(logical=False)`` reports locally "
"so the two paths are comparable.  ``NUMBER_OF_PROCESSORS`` is the "
"fallback: it counts *logical* processors and so over-estimates on an SMT "
"machine, which is the harmless direction — core counts are advisory here,"
" and licence tokens are the hard cap."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.probe_cores:10 of
msgid ""
"Returns ``None`` when neither answers, leaving the caller to insist on an"
" explicit ``HostSpec.cpus_total`` rather than run on a guess."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.submit_detached:1 of
msgid "Write a .bat wrapper, launch it via WMI, and return a pollable handle."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.submit_detached:3 of
msgid ""
"The command is *not* run through the SSH channel directly: see "
":mod:`~ABQflow.core.remote_launch` for why the solver has to outlive the "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.poll:1 of
msgid "Return the solver return code, or ``None`` while it is still running."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.poll:3 of
msgid ""
"Reconnects transparently: the answer is a file on the remote disk, so "
"losing the connection costs nothing but a retry."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.is_alive:1 of
msgid "Whether the launcher process still exists on the remote machine."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.is_alive:3 of
msgid ""
"Queried with ``tasklist /FI \"PID eq <pid>\"``, which prints a header and"
" the matching row, or an \"INFO: No tasks\" line when nothing matches.  "
"The PID is the ``cmd.exe`` running the launcher script, so its "
"disappearance means the script will never reach the line that writes the "
"rc sentinel — the job is over whether or not it succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.is_alive:9 of
msgid ""
"Returns ``None`` when the launcher reported no PID, or when the query "
"itself fails: a connection hiccup must not be mistaken for a dead job and"
" cut short a solve that has been running for hours."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.terminate:1 of
msgid "Remote mirror of the local escalation ladder."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.get:1 of
msgid "Download one file."
msgstr ""

#: ABQflow.core.backends.ssh.SshBackend.get:3 of
msgid ""
"SFTP is a **binary** transfer — no newline translation — so files arrive "
"exactly as Abaqus wrote them, which is what lets the unmodified "
"``.sta``/``.msg`` parsers run against them."
msgstr ""

